HR Analytics – Employee Attrition Analysis

Project Overview

This project analyzes employee attrition using HR data to identify patterns and understand employee turnover.

Project Objectives

- Analyze overall employee attrition.
- Identify departments with high attrition.
- Analyze job-role-wise attrition.
- Study overtime and job satisfaction.
- Provide business recommendations.

Dataset Information

- Dataset: IBM HR Employee Attrition Dataset
- Total Records: 1,470 employees
- Total Features: 35 columns
- Target Variable: Attrition

Tools & Technologies

- Python
- Google Colab
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn

Key Findings

- Sales department attrition: 20.63%
- Human Resources attrition: 19.05%
- Research & Development attrition: 13.84%
- Sales Representatives attrition: 39.76%

Business Recommendations

- Review sales targets and workload.
- Improve employee retention strategies.
- Monitor overtime and job satisfaction.
- Provide career development opportunities.

Conclusion

This project demonstrates how data analytics can help organizations understand employee attrition and improve workforce planning.

